symbol-reference sweep finds two further callers it omits: `create_session_log` (session_log.py:144) and `create_identity` (identity.py:298). Since the `duplicate_warning` is computed INSIDE `create_core`, both receive it; the identity path in particular reaches library `rebar.create_identity` and MCP `create_identity`, which returns the very `CreateResultOut` the plan extends with `duplicate_warning`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f203d23da511092f3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design → Surfacing (\"each surface emits it on its own channel\") and Portability (\"the single seam every create funnels through: CLI, library, MCP, idea()\")","norm_id":"n48af186ea83d25f5","priority":0.6667,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["MCP create_identity returns CreateResultOut (gaining a duplicate_warning field per the plan) but the plan never states whether that surface emits or suppresses the warning — an unaddressed surface.","create_session_log calls create_core and returns only {id, alias}, silently dropping any duplicate_warning — an inconsistent/unaddressed surface.","The 'single seam funnels through CLI, library, MCP, idea()' claim is factually incomplete, so a reviewer/implementer working from it under-inventories create_core call sites."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"insufficient","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"insufficient","impact_follows_necessarily":"insufficient","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"insufficient","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the create-time advisory duplicate-detection decision in an ADR (or an update to ADR 0086) recording the write-path journal design, the 600 s window rationale, and the advisory-not-blocking choice.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T7","T5e"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8086,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan invokes 'ADR 0086 placed the heavy overlap detector at review time, off the hot write path'","File impact lists only 'docs/config.md: note the create-time advisory' — no ADR file","This adds a second, create-time detection layer on the write path — a novel architectural decision distinct from the review-time detector"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new create-time detection mechanism (rolling recent-creates journal sidecar on the write path) that materially extends the architecture ADR 0086 established (which placed duplicate detection at review time), but proposes no ADR entry or update to ADR 0086 — only a docs/config.md note. The plan itself cites ADR 0086 as the governing decision record for where detection lives.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f192cda7e86e24d2c","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section / File impact (docs/config.md) — 'ADR 0086 placed the heavy overlap detector at review time, off the hot write path'","norm_id":"nf24261890905138f","priority":0.1414,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer reads ADR 0086, believes detection is review-time-only, and is surprised by write-path journal I/O","Someone revisits the create-time-vs-review-time split without a recorded rationale"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add an ADR entry (or amend ADR 0086) to file impact documenting the create-time journal sidecar as a deliberate second, cheap, advisory detection layer complementing the review-time overlap detector.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the fcntl dependency behaves on Windows — confirm the HLC precedent already gates fcntl (so the write path is already POSIX-only) or guard the fcntl import/lock so create degrades to no-warning rather than crashing on non-POSIX platforms.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the whole read-prune-probe-append-rewrite is one critical section under a dedicated exclusive `fcntl.flock`'","'`fcntl` matches the existing HLC-sidecar precedent in-tree.'","Platform matrix includes Windows; `import fcntl` raises ModuleNotFoundError on Windows"],"finding":"The mechanism mandates a dedicated exclusive `fcntl.flock` on `recent-creates.lock`, and `recent_creates.py` will import `fcntl`. `fcntl` is POSIX-only and absent on Windows (a supported platform), so importing the module raises ModuleNotFoundError. The plan grounds this on the in-tree HLC-sidecar precedent (`src/rebar/_store/hlc.py`) but does not confirm that precedent guards the import or that Windows is already unsupported for the write path — leaving whether this newly breaks Windows unstated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f985b100cfd9f50d0","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — Mechanism / Concurrency: 'a dedicated exclusive `fcntl.flock` on the sidecar `recent-creates.lock`' and Portability: '`fcntl` matches the existing HLC-sidecar precedent in-tree.'","norm_id":"nb45bdc99267587e6","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Windows platform: if `recent_creates.py` imports `fcntl` at module load and `composer.py` imports it unconditionally, `rebar create` fails at import time on Windows even with the flag off — a crash, not a degraded no-warning."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4444,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"insufficient"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Log the probe-degradation path (at debug/warning on the library logger) so a persistently failing journal is observable rather than a silent no-op, while still never failing the create.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6612,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["'Every probe failure (unreadable journal, config error, reduce failure) degrades to no-warning'","No mention of logging/recording the degradation path; the same paragraph routes success to logger but is silent on the failure path's observability"],"finding":"The plan degrades every probe failure (unreadable journal, config error, reduce failure) to no-warning, but does not instrument that degradation — no log/metric records that the advisory silently stopped working. A persistently corrupt or unwritable journal would suppress all duplicate warnings indefinitely with no operator-visible signal.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1d9429fa4c372582","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — Surfacing: 'Every probe failure ... degrades to no-warning — an advisory must never fail a completed write.'","norm_id":"nde29f73eef4e09d8","priority":0.2888,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A journal file that becomes unwritable (permissions/disk) makes every subsequent probe a silent no-op; operators never learn the feature stopped detecting duplicates."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Emit a debug/warning log entry on each caught probe failure (guarded so it cannot itself raise), distinct from the success-path logger call.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the 600 s window is an intentionally-fixed design constant or should be a named module-level constant / config knob, and record the decision (with the measured 171 s basis) so it is greppable and adjustable.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["'pruned to a fixed recency window (600 s ...)'","'no new config surface'"],"finding":"The 600 s recency window is hardcoded as a design constant with no configuration surface. The plan states 'no new config surface' and gates only on the existing boolean flag, so operators cannot tune the window if the empirically observed 171 s max delta shifts over time.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffd80ac3cf94980d6","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — Mechanism ('pruned to a fixed recency window (600 s, ~3.5x the largest observed true-duplicate delta of 171 s)') and Gating ('no new config surface')","norm_id":"n0a7cff0c1ac8723d","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Duplicate-burst timing changes in a busier project and the fixed 600 s window becomes too narrow or too wide"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Define the window as a named module-level constant in recent_creates.py with a comment tying it to the measured 171 s max delta, and note in docs whether tuning requires a code change; this keeps it changeable without a full config surface.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_wi